  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is an AI inference architecture that grounds large language model responses by dynamically fetching semantically relevant passages from an external knowledge store at query time. A retriever\u2014typically backed by a vector database using dense embeddings\u2014identifies the most relevant document chunks, which are concatenated into the model's context window before generation. RAG reduces hallucination, enables up-to-date knowledge without costly retraining, and allows fine-grained attribution of generated claims to source documents, making it the dominant pattern for enterprise knowledge-intensive question answering.",
